{#
    Shared Google-style (Napoleon-compatible) docstring formatting for generated
    client/server methods.

    Import into a template with:
        {% import "partials/docstrings.jinja2" as docstrings %}

    Imported macros do not inherit the calling template's context (globals like
    ``config``/``stinger`` are not visible), but attribute access on objects passed as
    arguments, and environment-registered filters such as ``snake_case``, work exactly
    as they do everywhere else -- so ``args`` can be a raw list of ``Arg`` objects
    rather than something the caller has to pre-flatten.
#}

{#
    Renders a docstring body: an optional summary, an optional ``extra`` prose block,
    an ``Args:`` section built from a raw list of ``Arg`` objects, an optional
    ``Returns:`` section from a caller-supplied ``(type_str, description)`` tuple, and
    an optional ``Raises:`` section from a list of such tuples.

    The whole body is assembled at a zero-indentation baseline and indented exactly
    once at the end. Black's docstring auto-formatter re-indents docstring bodies to
    match the enclosing code, so pre-indenting some lines (e.g. a multi-line summary)
    but not others (e.g. this macro's own "Args:" block) produces a mixed baseline
    that gets double-indented on the already-indented lines. ``indent_width`` should
    match the indentation of the ``def``/``class`` this docstring belongs to (4 for a
    top-level function, 8 for a method on a class, ...).
#}
{%- macro google_docstring(summary, indent_width, args=[], returns=none, extra=none, raises=[]) -%}
{%- set body %}
{%- if summary %}{{ summary }}
{% endif -%}
{%- if extra %}
{{ extra }}
{% endif -%}
{%- if args | length > 0 %}
Args:
{% for arg in args %}    {{ arg.name | snake_case }} ({{ arg.python.annotation }}): {{ arg.description or "No description provided." }}
{% endfor -%}
{% endif -%}
{%- if returns %}
Returns:
    {{ returns[0] }}: {{ returns[1] or "No description provided." }}
{% endif -%}
{%- if raises | length > 0 %}
Raises:
{% for exc in raises %}    {{ exc[0] }}: {{ exc[1] or "No description provided." }}
{% endfor -%}
{% endif -%}
{%- endset %}
{{- body | indent(indent_width) }}
{%- endmacro -%}
